        ":question/problem": "Find the value of $x$ that satisfies the equation ${8}^{x}\\cdot {4}^{2x-1}=32.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To solve this equation, we need both exponential terms to have a common base. To do this, we rewrite the equation using $8={2}^{3}$, $4={2}^{2}$ and $32={2}^{5},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{({2}^{3})}^{x}\\cdot {({2}^{2})}^{2x-1}={2}^{5}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule and the product rule of exponents. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{3x}\\cdot {2}^{2(2x-1)} & ={2}^{5} \\\\ {2}^{3x+2(2x-1)} & ={2}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(2)$, we equate the exponents and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2(2x-1) & =5 \\\\ 3x+4x-2 & =5 \\\\ 7x & =7 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
